00:16:21.813 --> 00:16:23.548 align:start size:69% position:31%
All right, verdict.
What are you thinking?

00:16:23.581 --> 00:16:25.183 align:start position:0%
It's pretty dope.

00:16:25.216 --> 00:16:26.719 align:start size:34% position:66%
Super dope.

00:16:28.686 --> 00:16:31.056
Marques:
<i> Polaroid's innovation
 not only inspired</i>

00:16:31.089 --> 00:16:35.060
<i> both amateur
 and professional photographers
 in the '70s and '80s,</i>

00:16:35.093 --> 00:16:37.696
<i> but years later,
 it was the catchy lyrics
 of a hit song</i>

00:16:37.729 --> 00:16:41.299
<i> that would inspire a new wave
 of Polaroid enthusiasts.</i>

00:16:41.332 --> 00:16:44.770
In 2003, OutKast came out
with the infamous "Hey Ya!"

00:16:44.803 --> 00:16:47.739 line:0%
<i> It brought so much attention
 to Polaroid as a company.</i>

00:16:47.772 --> 00:16:50.642 line:0%
♪ Shake it like
a Polaroid picture ♪

00:16:50.675 --> 00:16:53.311 line:0%
<i> Polaroid was like,
 "This is great,</i>

00:16:53.344 --> 00:16:57.182 line:0%
<i> but you also shouldn't
 actually shake the Polaroid."</i>

00:16:57.215 --> 00:16:59.284
You should not shake it
like a Polaroid picture.

00:16:59.317 --> 00:17:00.652
- Don't shake it.
- Don't shake it.

00:17:00.685 --> 00:17:02.254
Don't shake the picture,
you'll just crack it.

00:17:06.324 --> 00:17:09.361
I was today years old
when I found out

00:17:09.394 --> 00:17:10.729
that you're not supposed
to shake it

00:17:10.762 --> 00:17:12.397
like a Polaroid picture.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.399 align:start size:66% position:34%
But I blame Polaroid.

00:17:14.432 --> 00:17:16.768
Polaroid should've said,
"André 3000, shut up.

00:17:16.801 --> 00:17:18.703
That's not what you're supposed
to do, Mr. Benjamin."

00:17:18.736 --> 00:17:20.572
♪ Leave it, leave it, leave it ♪

00:17:20.605 --> 00:17:23.175
♪ Leave it on the table
like a Polaroid picture ♪

00:17:23.208 --> 00:17:26.778
But that's not catchy,
and that wouldn't
have went platinum.

00:17:26.811 --> 00:17:30.282 line:0%
 Marques:<i> The OutKast song
 "Hey Ya!" was a huge hit,</i>

00:17:30.315 --> 00:17:34.152 line:0%
<i> and despite the bad advice,
 Polaroid scored some
 major publicity.</i>

00:17:34.185 --> 00:17:36.721 line:0%
<i> But even that wouldn't
 be enough to protect them</i>

00:17:36.754 --> 00:17:39.224 line:0%
<i> from an oncoming
 digital revolution.</i>

